      "writtenOn": "2025-09-12T20:36:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, the problem I described is with the internal R001 swizzle, not with the swizzle feature since that\u0027s validated. I\u0027ve gone through the latest logic and I think it handles that correctly.\n\nHowever, now I\u0027m realizing there may be a problem with the swizzle feature too: Metal cannot create views with a subset of usages. The spec allows creating a texture with `RENDER_ATTACHMENT | TEXTURE_BINDING` and then creating a view with a swizzle if the view usage is only `TEXTURE_BINDING`. But the Metal view still has all usages, so Metal may not allow this.\n\nWe need to make sure that this is tested.",
      "parentUuid": "9ee3d5a2_247da46d",
      "revId": "17896857fef0d1f70b34f97f1ee34c67926fcd78",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
